6674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (You can use a column's number \(where the leftmost column is '1'\) to indicate which column to base the sort on, instead of describing the column by its name. Pro: If you think it's likely you might change column names later, doing so won't break this code. Con: This will generally reduce readability of the query \(It's instantly clear what 'ORDER BY  Reputation' means, while 'ORDER BY 14' requires some counting, probably with a finger on the  screen.\) This query sorts result by the info in relative column position 3 from select statement instead of  column name Reputation.)
